.TH LINEAR 1 2000-1月 "intervene" "intervene"
.SH NAME
intervene \- Run one in silico perturbation experiment and return the raw result object.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIintervene(\fBmodel\fR as <generic> ElasticNet, 
\fBgene\fR as string, 
\fBmode\fR as string = "knockout", 
\fBvalue\fR as double = 0, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Run one in silico perturbation experiment and return the raw result object.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBmodel\fB \fR\- the perturbation engine that is created via \fBelastic_model\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgene\fB \fR\- the target gene id. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmode\fB \fR\- \fBknockout\fR, \fBknockdown\fR, \fBoverexpress\fR or \fBcustom\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBvalue\fB \fR\- 
 the absolute expression value in the model space, only used by the \fBcustom\fR mode.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
an [InterventionResult](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.BioSystem.Intervention.InterventionResult) object; use \fBas.list\fR to access the fields
 (the \fB$\fR indexing is not supported on this object).
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
linear
.SH FILES
.PP
TRNtoolkit.dll
.PP
